# Mizu UI & Layout Rules

Adhere strictly to these spatial layout, alignment, and Compose architecture guidelines across all UI components and screens.

## 1. The 2× Proximity & Spacing Law (`better-layout`)
- Group elements with whitespace first, background shapes second, and separator lines last.
- The gap between two distinct groups must be **at least double (2×)** the gap inside a single group.
  - Internal item spacing (title to subtitle): `4.dp` or `8.dp`
  - Gap between distinct items/cards: `16.dp` minimum.
- Eliminate hairline horizontal dividers between cards; let negative space and card boundaries define separation.

## 2. Touch Target Floor & Ergonomics (`mobile-design`)
- Every interactive element (buttons, chips, list items, icons) must have a minimum hit area of **48×48dp**.
- Adjacent touch targets must maintain at least **8dp** of spacing to prevent accidental touches.
- Destructive actions (Delete, Clear) must never sit near natural thumb resting zones or right next to high-frequency buttons.

## 3. Compose Modifier Ordering Standard
Always chain modifiers in this exact sequence to ensure correct hit boundaries, clipping, and shadows:
```kotlin
Modifier
    .fillMaxWidth()                  // 1. Structural constraints
    .neoShadow(...)                  // 2. Outer drop shadow
    .border(...)                     // 3. Structural boundary / ink stroke
    .clip(shape)                     // 4. Shape clipping
    .background(color)               // 5. Background fill
    .clickable(...)                  // 6. Interaction (covers full outer bounds)
    .padding(internalPadding)        // 7. Internal content inset
```

## 4. Concentric Corner Radii (`better-ui`)
- When nesting rounded elements inside a card with padding `P`:
  `R_outer = R_inner + P`
- Keep corner radii mathematically concentric to avoid awkward visual dissonance.

## 5. Tablet & Adaptive Layouts (Xiaomi Pad 6)
- Compact (< 600dp width): Bottom navigation bar, 1-column list or 2-column video grid.
- Expanded (> 840dp width): Navigation rail, adaptive grid (`GridCells.Adaptive(minSize = 220.dp)`), and master/detail split where appropriate.
- Always apply `WindowInsets.safeDrawing` or `safeContent` to avoid camera cutouts and gesture bars.
